 =?UTF-8?q?achine?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
- Place the machine row above the project list, directly below Search, as a full-width dropdown. Display it only with at least two known environments; otherwise ignore saved machine scope.
- Display All machines for an empty effective set, one machine's icon and name for a singleton, or every selected icon followed by comma-joined names with ellipsis and a full-name tooltip. List checkbox choices primary first, followed by catalog order; plain mouse or keyboard picks select one machine (or clear a repeated singleton) and close the menu; Cmd-click on macOS / Ctrl-click elsewhere adds or removes one machine and keeps the menu open. Cancel macOS Ctrl-click on machine items without changing selection, clear through a plain All machines action followed by a separator, and normalize selecting every known machine to empty. Machines have no Hide mode. Modifier handling uses the native mouse event directly; keyboard activation and drag-release clicks select normally.
- Persist sidebarEnvironmentScopeKeys as a sanitized array, migrating the legacy null/single sidebarEnvironmentScopeKey. Keep unknown saved keys but ignore them for display and filtering; a set with no known member behaves as All machines.
- Combine machine membership with project scope: threads must belong to any selected machine and an allowed project. A logical project remains available if any member belongs to any selected machine. Resolve selected project keys against available groups without erasing saved keys that are temporarily absent; an empty effective project intersection behaves as all projects.
- Apply the same scope to thread partitions, drafts, empty-draft counts, search environment requests, settled pagination/counts, folder inputs and keyboard/jump order. Reset the settled tail when the project or machine set changes, using a stable set key.
- For exactly one selected machine, rebuild project metadata through upstream grouping from original records ordered by member refs, preserving historical IDs and repository fallback across same-path deduplication. Refs, favicons, settings targets, labels and presence describe that machine. With several selected machines, retain All-machines metadata for groups with a member on any selected machine.
- Reuse the shared environment membership predicate in production group filtering.
- Preserve folders, delegated-thread nesting, F6/DOM navigation and desktop history. Route reveal clears a machine set only when it hides the opened thread, without unnecessarily widening the project dimension; archived/nested rows do not spuriously widen scopes.
- Clear multi-thread selection on explicit scope changes, name selected machines together in empty states, and allow independent clearing of project and machine filters. Web, Electron renderer and mobile browser share the feature; native mobile, server/provider protocols and contracts are unchanged.
- When the machine filter spans more than one machine (All machines with two or more known, or two or more selected), every thread row's second line shows the thread's machine with its icon instead of the branch, replacing the rule that showed it only for No project threads (apps/web/src/components/sidebar/SidebarThreadRow.tsx, covered by apps/web/src/components/sidebar/SidebarThreadRow.browser.test.tsx).

Integration details:
- Compose with upstream pinned/archived project grouping, pinned empty folders, reorder safeguards, accessible row navigation, quiet draft subscriptions and route hover reveal. Explicit machine changes reset sidebar scroll; the upstream draft browser fixture takes the machine-scope input.
- Machine scope composes with the upstream sidebar partition restored by the offline Working shelf revert (#31269).

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. 965ddc1d6c has no machine filter of its own.

Port to e07585e5fb:
- SidebarThreadRow.tsx: upstream #34878 renders the branch from checkoutThread, which drops a deleted branch and worktree. The machine line still takes precedence over the branch; the branch fallback and the empty-line check now read checkoutThread.
- Sidebar.tsx: upstream #35426 moved the empty state above the thread list, shows it when a project scope hides every active thread and offers Show all projects. That state now names the selected machines too: sidebarEmptyThreadsLabel gains hasSettledThreads for upstream's "No active threads in <project>" wording (the machine suffix follows the project), and the unscoped fallback still names the machines. Added a row for it in sidebarEnvironmentScope.test.ts.

